From e918391fbf0914c6284e7407fae22332282fc127 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shkosugi <sin.kosugi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:42:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Type names without an assembly: System.Web's and mscorlib's,
 as Type.GetType has them

The type resolvers given to Type.GetType returned null for a name without an assembly
(asm?.GetType(...)), where .NET Framework's Type.GetType(name) looks in the calling assembly
and mscorlib. machine.config names its modules so (System.Web.Security.UrlAuthorizationModule):
UrlAuthorizationModule.CheckUrlAccessForPrincipal found no UrlAuthorizationModule registered and
allowed every path - a route to a page (FriendlyUrls, PageRouteHandler) was not authorized, and
the site map's security trimming showed every node. Without an assembly, Type.GetType resolves
the name as .NET Framework did, everywhere the pattern was.
